{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And you shall set a space between drove and drove</b> — in order to satisfy the eye of that wicked man and to make him wonder at the gift. And the Sages in Bereshit Rabbah (75:13) held that there is a hint in this: Jacob said before the Holy One, blessed be He, Master of the universe, if troubles come upon my children, do not bring them one after another, but give them relief from their troubles. He made a hint that the taxes and the imposts that the children of Esau will exact from his seed will come with relief and interval, one separated from the other."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:38:37.158823095Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}